  "name": "Question 3",
  "problem": "Arranged in **ascending order**, the solutions of the equation $\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}$ for ${0}^{\u2218}<x\\le {360}^{\u2218},$ are $x=${{field-1}}${}^{\u2218}$ and $x=$\n{{field-2}}${}^{\u2218}.$",
  "worked_solution": "First, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=\\operatorname{arccos}\u2061(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2})={30}^{\u2218}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince ${30}^{\u2218}$ lies inside the required domain, our first solution is ${x}_{1}={30}^{\u2218}.$\n\nOur first solution lies in the first quadrant and has a reference angle of ${\\theta }_{R}={30}^{\u2218}.$ Since $\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x>0,$ the second solution must lie in the fourth quadrant, and it also has a reference angle ${\\theta }_{R}={30}^{\u2218}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13952163/assets/d88379fcad6ee1bfc7f6c2159c814f92ca330dbacee191ebebb027bab306fe2c.png)\n\nSince the second solution ${x}_{2}$ lies in the $4$th quadrant, we can find it using the reference angle as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} & ={360}^{\u2218}-{\\theta }_{R} \\\\  & ={360}^{\u2218}-{30}^{\u2218} \\\\  & ={330}^{\u2218}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solutions of the equation, arranged in ascending order, are $x={30}^{\u2218}$ and $x={330}^{\u2218}.$",
